{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Polynomial.Cyclotomic.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Circle","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.Polynomial.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.ComputeDegree","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":28,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.C6core_non_cyclotomic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.C6core_non_cyclotomic","kind":"theorem","line":324,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.lean#L324-L357","doc":"**Conclusion (sorry-free modulo `Ctil_has_nonreal_root`)** — `C₆` is not a\nproduct of cyclotomic polynomials.  This needs only the *easy* direction of\nKronecker's dichotomy: every root of a product of cyclotomics is a root of\nunity (`cyclotomic k ∣ Xᵏ − 1`), hence has norm 1 — contradicting the\noff-circle root from `C6core_offcircle_root`.  (The hard Kronecker converse,\nabsent from Mathlib, is *not* used.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.C6core_offcircle_root","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.C6core_offcircle_root","kind":"theorem","line":290,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.lean#L290-L322","doc":"**Reduction (sorry-free)** — there is a root of `C₆` off the unit circle,\nreduced to `Ctil_has_nonreal_root` alone.  A non-real root `y` of `C̃` lifts,\nvia `z = (y + w)/2` with `w² = y² − 4`, to a nonzero `z` with `z + z⁻¹ = y`\nand `C6ℂ z = z⁴·C̃(y) = 0` (`C6_reciprocal`); and `‖z‖ ≠ 1`, else\n`unit_circle_sum_real` forces `y = z + z⁻¹` real, contradicting `y.im ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.Ctil_has_nonreal_root","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.Ctil_has_nonreal_root","kind":"theorem","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.lean#L232-L288","doc":"**`C̃` has a non-real root** (sorry-free).  `C̃ = X⁴+4X³+2X²−10X−8` is monic\nof degree 4, so over `ℂ` it splits into four roots `a,b,c,d`\n(`IsAlgClosed.splits_codomain` + `eq_prod_roots_of_monic_of_splits_id`).  If\nall four were real, Vieta gives `Σ = −4, Σ₂ = 2, Σ₃ = 10, Π = −8`, whence\n`Ctil_no_four_real_roots` derives `False` from `Δ(C̃) = −44208 < 0`.  So some\nroot has nonzero imaginary part.  This is the classical fact\n`Δ < 0 ⇒` non-real root, here proved from scratch (Mathlib has no quartic\ndiscriminant bridge) via the explicit 16-term symmetric identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.Ctil_no_four_real_roots","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.Ctil_no_four_real_roots","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.lean#L212-L230","doc":"Quartic discriminant identity `∏_{i<j}(rᵢ−rⱼ)² = Δ(C̃)` written in the\nelementary symmetric functions of `a,b,c,d` (16 terms; a pure `ring`\nidentity), evaluated at the Vieta values of `C̃`: if four reals are the\nroots of `C̃` (`Σ = −4`, `Σ₂ = 2`, `Σ₃ = 10`, `Π = −8`) then their\nVandermonde square equals `Δ(C̃) = −44208 < 0` (`Ctil_disc`) — impossible,\nsince a Vandermonde square of reals is `≥ 0`.  Hence `C̃` has no four real\nroots. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.Ctil_disc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.Ctil_disc","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.lean#L207-L209","doc":"The discriminant datum `Δ(C̃) = −44208 < 0` (computed; certifies the two\ncomplex roots of `C̃`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.unit_circle_sum_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.unit_circle_sum_real","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.lean#L196-L205","doc":"If `‖z‖ = 1` then `z + z⁻¹` is real (its imaginary part vanishes, since\n`z⁻¹ = conj z`).  Fully proved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.C6_reciprocal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.C6_reciprocal","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.lean#L189-L194","doc":"Palindrome identity `C₆(z) = z⁴·C̃(z + z⁻¹)` for every nonzero `z`.  Fully proved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.C6ℂ_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.C6ℂ_eq","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.lean#L181-L187","doc":"`C6ℂ` really is `C6core` evaluated over `ℂ` (so the off-circle root below is a\nroot of the integer polynomial `C6core`).  Fully proved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.Ctilℂ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.Ctilℂ","kind":"def","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.lean#L178-L179","doc":"`C̃` as an explicit `ℂ`-valued function. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.C6ℂ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.C6ℂ","kind":"def","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.lean#L173-L176","doc":"`C₆` as an explicit `ℂ`-valued function (= `C6core` evaluated over `ℂ`, see\n`C6ℂ_eq`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.Ctil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.Ctil","kind":"def","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.lean#L170-L171","doc":"The reduced quartic `C̃(y) = y⁴ + 4y³ + 2y² − 10y − 8`, from `C₆(q) = q⁴·C̃(q+q⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.D5_cyclotomic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.D5_cyclotomic","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.lean#L163-L166","doc":"`D(5)` is a product of cyclotomic polynomials (Tier 1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.D4_cyclotomic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.D4_cyclotomic","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.lean#L159-L161","doc":"`D(4)` is a product of cyclotomic polynomials (Tier 1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.Phi6_cyclotomic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.Phi6_cyclotomic","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.lean#L130-L157","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.Phi5_cyclotomic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.Phi5_cyclotomic","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.lean#L123-L128","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.Phi3_cyclotomic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.Phi3_cyclotomic","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.lean#L116-L121","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.Phi2_cyclotomic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.Phi2_cyclotomic","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.lean#L113-L114","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.Phi1_cyclotomic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.Phi1_cyclotomic","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.lean#L110-L111","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.D5_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.D5_eq","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.lean#L104-L106","doc":"`D(5) = 2 · Φ₁² · Φ₂² · Φ₃ · Φ₆`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.D4_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.D4_eq","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.lean#L100-L102","doc":"`D(4) = Φ₁² · Φ₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.Phi6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.Phi6","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.lean#L96-L96","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.Phi5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.Phi5","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.lean#L95-L95","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.Phi3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.Phi3","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.lean#L94-L94","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.Phi2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.Phi2","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.lean#L93-L93","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.Phi1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.Phi1","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.lean#L91-L92","doc":"Explicit cyclotomic factors used in the base cases. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.C6core","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.C6core","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.lean#L87-L89","doc":"The non-cyclotomic degree-8 core of `D(6)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.D5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.D5","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.lean#L84-L85","doc":"`D(5)` stripped: `2X⁸ − 2X⁶ − 2X² + 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.D4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.D4","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CyclotomicBoundaryKeystone.lean#L81-L82","doc":"`D(4)` stripped: `X⁴ − X³ − X + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}